   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to the release of dogs and cats to a pound, shelter, society for the prevention of cruelty to animals, duly incorporated humane society or duly incorporated animal protective association in certain cases",
    "basePrintNo": "S5794",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5794-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§374 & 118, Ag & Mkts L",
    "lawSection": "Agriculture and Markets Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5794\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to the\nrelease of dogs and cats to a pound, shelter, society for the\nprevention of cruelty to animals, duly incorporated humane society or\nduly incorporated animal protective association in certain cases\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nTo allow the release of dogs and cats to other entities in addition to\nadoptees or owners to increase chances for adoption.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nThis bill amends subdivision 2-e and paragraph b of subdivision 5 of\nsection 374 and subdivision 7-a of section 118 of the agriculture and\nmarkets law to provide that a pound, shelter, society for the\nprevention of cruelty of animals, humane society, dog protective\nassociation, dog control officer, peace officer or any agent thereof\nmay release a dog or cat to another pound, shelter, society for the\nprevention of cruelty of animals, duly incorporated humane society or\nduly incorporated animal protective association if such action is\nreasonably likely to create an opportunity for the adoption of such\ndog or cat within a reasonable period of time.\n\n EFFECTS OF PRESENT LAW WHICH THIS BILL WOULD ALTER :\nUnder existing law, shelters may only release a dog or cat for\nadoption or redemption by the animal's owner. It does not allow a\nshelter to transfer animals to any of the above-named\nentities/persons, although such authorization would considerably\nenhance an animal's chance for adoption.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis legislation will ensure that whenever there are areas of the\nstate which experience increased demand for dogs or cats and the\nsupply of such animals is readily abundant in other areas of the\nstate, other animal shelter-type entities may transport such animals\nto another shelter and release the animals to that shelter for the\npurpose of facilitating adoption.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2007-2008:  A.519 Referred to Agriculture\n2005-2006:  A.3990 Referred to Agriculture\n2003-2004:  A.374 Referred to Agriculture\n2001-2002:  Referred to Agriculture and Markers\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\n60th day after enactment.\n",
